.SS "virtual \fBvoid\fP Assimp::LogStream::write (const char * message)\fR [pure virtual]\fP"

.PP
Overwrite this for your own output methods\&. Log messages \fImay\fP consist of multiple lines and you shouldn't expect a consistent formatting\&. If you want custom formatting (e\&.g\&. generate HTML), supply a custom instance of \fBLogger\fP to #DefaultLogger:set()\&. Usually you can \fIexpect\fP that a log message is exactly one line and terminated with a single 
.br
 character\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImessage\fP Message to be written 
.RE
